exec(compile(open('/tmp/legal-refusal-recovery-j_10md5l/install_checkpoint.py').read().split('originals = ')[0], '<load-source-control>', 'exec'))
descriptor=json.loads((BASE/'evidence-descriptor.json').read_bytes())
docs=ROOT/'ipfs_datasets_py/logic/autoformal'
paths=[docs/'README.md',docs/'docs/HANDOFF.md',docs/'docs/OPERATIONS.md',docs/'docs/work_catalog.json']
originals={p:p.read_bytes() for p in paths};updates={}
p=paths[0];text=originals[p].decode()
needle='See [operations](docs/OPERATIONS.md#agent-owner-pauses-and-independent-continuations).'
assert text.count(needle)==1
updates[p]=text.replace(needle,needle+' Exact provider-turn observations can now be ingested into a durable continuation checkpoint, retaining refusal evidence, spent attempts and both histories. The local owning suite passed 95 tests and 171 subtests; rejected operations remain held.').encode()
p=paths[1];text=originals[p].decode();assert text.startswith('# Current handoff\n')
note='''
## Provider-turn continuation checkpoint — local software change

The existing `agent-turn-recovery` command now accepts `--observation` for an already charged task and its exact original thread/turn. It preserves provider errors/evidence and emits `next_frontier` with policy holds and both histories. Cleanup and acceptance require explicit independent evidence; terminal provider status does not release an unknown Source/process/resource scope. Rejected operations, aliases and unaccepted dependents remain held, while independent already-authorized tasks retain existing scope, capacity and pause/usage checks. Dispatch, retry, resume, goal mutation and admission flags remain false.

Observation mode requires an exclusive checkpoint output. Success follows file and directory fsync plus identity rechecks. Failed writes preserve partial artifacts and return failure; filename existence alone is not commit. The caller retains the whole checkpoint and compares its consumed-frontier digest before existing atomic claim/admission.

All 95 local owning unit/CLI tests and 171 subtests passed, zero failures/errors/skips: 67 retained tests plus 28 new controls. Source hashes remained unchanged and the Source READ closed. Limits were one CPU, 60 CPU/wall seconds and 512MiB address space. Independent static review found three issues fixed before qualification: digesting mutable input twice, allowing refusal-evidence rewrites, and missing post-directory-sync identity checks. The tests cover those findings, duplicate events, wrong owners, unknown cleanup, failed syncs and retained budget/policy barriers. This isolated branch is not published and does not execute a live provider request, replay a rejected operation, change a host goal, or qualify Native Lean, statutory meaning, model training or corpus admission. The earlier 67-test record and broader failed runs remain historical.

'''
note+='Local evidence: `'+descriptor['path']+'` ('+str(descriptor['bytes'])+' bytes / SHA256 `'+descriptor['sha256']+'`).\n\n'
updates[p]=text.replace('# Current handoff\n','# Current handoff\n\n'+note,1).encode()
p=paths[2];text=originals[p].decode();anchor='## CLI4 separate original custody and retained failures'
assert text.count(anchor)==1
addition='''### Ingest an observed provider turn

Use the same owner and existing V2 frontier:

```sh
python scripts/ops/legal_ir/run_autoformal_supervisor.py agent-turn-recovery \\
  --inputs frontier.json --observation owner-turn.json --output checkpoint.json
```

`owner-turn.json` has exactly these fields, using actual original IDs/error and
saved evidence references:

```json
{
  "schema": "legal-ir-agent-turn-observation/v1",
  "task_id": "existing-task",
  "thread_id": "existing-thread",
  "turn": {"id": "existing-turn", "status": "failed", "error": {"code": "policy_refusal", "message": "Original refusal"}},
  "cleanup_confirmed": false,
  "accepted": false,
  "evidence_refs": []
}
```

The task must already have a charged attempt and a matching current or retained
owner observation. Supported provider states are `inProgress`, `completed`,
`failed` and `interrupted`; absent/ambiguous state is not terminal. Cleanup and
acceptance are never inferred. Keep them false without the existing owner's
independent evidence. Live owners remain exact polling targets. A refusal and its
original evidence stay held across aliases, resume directives and duplicate
delivery; explicit pauses and run-wide usage/resource holds remain effective.

Retain the whole output and pass its `next_frontier` into the next existing
scheduling call. It includes the updated observation, policy holds and both
histories; exact duplicate events preserve spent counters and the next frontier.
Verify `observation_checkpoint.input_frontier_sha256` against the current immutable
frontier before existing atomic claim/admission. Event and next-frontier digests
are also included. This adapter does not authenticate its own provider metadata
or mutate the task/goal store.

Observation mode requires `--output`; the three paths must differ. Output creation
is exclusive, with file and directory fsync and post-sync identity checks before
success. Failure returns code 2, starts no work and may leave a partial output.
Preserve it: existence alone is not a successful commit, and failed output must
not drive a claim or automatic repeat. Existing planning-only stdout mode remains
unchanged when `--observation` is absent. Local software qualification passed 95
tests and 171 subtests; no live provider recovery was performed.

'''
updates[p]=text.replace(anchor,addition+anchor,1).encode()
p=paths[3];data=json.loads(originals[p])
c=next(c for c in data['components'] if c['id']=='supervisor-handoff-preflight')
assert 'agent_turn_observation_checkpoint_v1' not in c
c['agent_turn_observation_checkpoint_v1']={'api':'prepare_agent_turn_recovery_checkpoint_v1',
 'cli':'scripts/ops/legal_ir/run_autoformal_supervisor.py agent-turn-recovery --inputs frontier.json --observation owner-turn.json --output checkpoint.json',
 'evidence':descriptor,'qualification':'95 local owning tests and 171 subtests passed; Source READ closed.',
 'publication_status':'local_branch_not_published',
 'scope':'Existing-turn metadata ingestion and durable checkpoint only; no provider authentication, retry, dispatch, goal mutation, runtime or legal admission.',
 'task_component_selected_evidence_populations_unchanged':True}
assert len(data['components'])==126 and len(data['selected_evidence'])==580
text=originals[p].decode()
marker='"id": "supervisor-handoff-preflight"'
assert text.count(marker)==1
start=text.rfind('\n    {',0,text.index(marker))+5
old_component,consumed=json.JSONDecoder().raw_decode(text[start:])
assert old_component['id']=='supervisor-handoff-preflight'
position=text.rfind('\n    }',start,start+consumed)
assert text[position:start+consumed]=='\n    }'
field='agent_turn_observation_checkpoint_v1'
fragment='\n'.join('    '+line for line in json.dumps({field:c[field]},sort_keys=True,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False).splitlines()[1:-1])
insertion=',\n'+fragment
new_text=text[:position]+insertion+text[position:]
assert new_text[:position]+new_text[position+len(insertion):]==text
assert json.loads(new_text)==data
updates[p]=new_text.encode()
with module.source_lease(ROOT,mode='write',timeout_seconds=30) as lease:
 for p,before in originals.items():assert p.read_bytes()==before
 for p,raw in updates.items():p.write_bytes(raw)
 for p,raw in updates.items():assert p.read_bytes()==raw
 facts=lease.to_dict()
print(json.dumps({'Source_WRITE_closed':True,'lease':facts,'evidence':descriptor,'docs':[{'path':str(p),'bytes':len(raw),'sha256':hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()} for p,raw in updates.items()]}))
